Subject: [PATCH] glamor: Skip core debug callbacks on Mali Utgard

The Utgard DDK exposes KHR-only debug entry points. Calling the core debug
callbacks during glamor initialization can jump to NULL. The existing
Utgard workaround disables has_khr_debug later, but the setup function
checks extensions directly and is called before that workaround.

Skip debug callback setup for Utgard, leaving acceleration enabled.

--- a/glamor/glamor.c
+++ b/glamor/glamor.c
@@ -840,7 +840,9 @@
 
     glamor_priv->can_copyplane = (gl_version >= 30);
 
-    glamor_setup_debug_output(screen);
+    /* Utgard exposes KHR-only debug entry points; skip core debug callbacks. */
+    if (!glamor_priv->is_utgard)
+        glamor_setup_debug_output(screen);
 
     glamor_priv->use_quads = !glamor_priv->is_gles &&
                              !glamor_priv->is_core_profile;
